            <ArticleTitle>Determining the optimal cutoff points for waist circumference and body mass index for identification of metabolic abnormalities and metabolic syndrome in urban Thai population.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e16-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2012.09.018</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0168-8227(12)00322-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study describes the prevalence and optimal waist circumference (WC) and body mass index (BMI) cutoff point for metabolic abnormalities and metabolic syndrome (MS) from urban Thai population. The optimal BMI/WC cutoff has been used for identifying and evaluating metabolic abnormalities for screening individuals having risk factor of MS.</AbstractText>
